From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kan Zhu <kanzhu@cs.washington.edu>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:40:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(alignment): rebase onto nightly 9d547e19 and pin the
 base in ALIGNMENT_BASE

vibesim-alignment-20261108 is vibesim-alignment-20261107 rebased from main
ba5906471c onto 9d547e19ff, the commit behind the official image
lmsysorg/sglang:nightly-dev-cu13-20261108-9d547e19. All seven commits
applied without conflicts.

ALIGNMENT_BASE names the upstream commit, the official image and its
manifest digest, so the Sim's profiler-image build reads the base instead of
inferring it from commit messages.

Both alignment forks (vLLM and SGLang) are now the latest upstream commit
plus its official image plus our commits. At the next upgrade, prefer a
stable release and its image.

ALIGNMENT.md lists the nine upstream commits since the last base and why
none needs the GLM-5.2 capture rerun: none touches the scheduler,
tokenizer_manager, the JIT cache, DSA/MoE kernels, or the NVTX/profiler
paths. The ROCm all-reduce change edits a JIT header under USE_ROCM, which
only changes that module's cache key on CUDA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
